---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Rules & Regulations" description="A practical introduction to the rules and records involved in keeping Portland sheep.">
  <div class="bg-sage-800 text-white py-20 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-sage-300 text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Husbandry</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl mb-6">Rules &amp; Regulations</h1>
      <p class="text-cream-200 text-xl max-w-2xl">The essential registrations, identification and records involved in keeping sheep.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-2xl p-5 mb-10 text-sm text-amber-900">
      Regulations change and differ across England, Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland. This page is an introduction, not legal advice. Always check the current guidance issued by the authority responsible for livestock in your nation.
    </div>
    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-sage-800">
      <h2>Before keeping sheep</h2>
      <p>You will normally need to register the land and the location at which livestock are kept. Keep the identifiers issued for the holding safe and use them on movement and flock records as required.</p>

      <h2>Identification</h2>
      <p>Sheep must be identified with approved tags within the applicable time limits and before leaving the holding. Requirements vary by age, destination and nation, so buy tags from an approved supplier and follow current official guidance.</p>

      <h2>Movements and records</h2>
      <p>Record arrivals, departures, births, deaths and replacement identifiers in the flock register. Movements between holdings generally need to be reported through the relevant national service, with accompanying documentation where required.</p>

      <h2>Welfare and medicines</h2>
      <p>Keepers are responsible for suitable feed, water, shelter and prompt treatment of illness or injury. Veterinary medicines must be stored, administered and recorded correctly, including the required withdrawal periods for meat and other products.</p>

      <h2>Breed registration</h2>
      <p>Legal livestock identification is separate from pedigree registration. Contact the Group for current information about registering eligible Portland sheep in the appropriate flock book and for advice on kinship before planning matings.</p>

      <h2>Ask before moving stock</h2>
      <p>If you are uncertain, contact the relevant government livestock service, your local authority animal-health team or your vet before buying, selling or moving animals.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
